// A mapped stdlib extern that FAULTS.
//
// `Int.pow` with an exponent whose power would not fit in memory is a
// runtime error. A builtin's own text names no line, so the report puts the
// line of the program's call in front of it, as for any trap inside the
// stdlib, and the words after it reach the user VERBATIM. So the text is a
// contract rt owns, and the `Int.pow:` qualification (which `Int.shift_left`'s
// does NOT share) is part of it rather than something to tidy.
//
// The print before the fault is the other half of the fixture: stdout must carry
// `before` before the error reaches stderr, which is what rt.Print
// writing unbuffered straight to fd 1 buys.
import std::io

fn main()
    io.print("before")
    io.inspect(Int.pow(3, 100_000_000_000))
end
